Z||000024||BAM-BAM||10-28-2000||08:22 AM||||   Count, that is BBBAD GT's 84 with a Chevy 350. It was built by a gentleman named Chris McDonald. The roof section is painted black. That has got to be truly the finest Fiero I have seen also. Now, Archie's White IMSA is bang'n too. Archie has some awesome cars and from what I can tell, does some awesome V8 conversions. That's what I have grown to love about the Fiero, Versitility. My plans for my 85GT are similar to BBBAD's red 84 in as far as the paint and wheels. I will be painting mine the 2000 Lexus silver with the black roof section. The wheel's I have chosen are MOMO EVO-3's<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/evo3_1.jpg"> <P>in 17"x8". I am still undecided on the engine, but I'm leaning towars a 3.4L HO. interior is almost ready to put together. It will be a blast to see it finished. I hope this helps you in your decision. Notchbacks are fun to work with but fastbacks look....well, FAST!  Have fun.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
